menu "RTPS Example Configuration"

    config RTPS_EXAMPLE_ANNOUNCE_PERIOD_MS
        int "Publish period (ms)"
        range 200 60000
        default 1500
        help
            Period between outgoing messages published by the MCU.

    config RTPS_EXAMPLE_SECOND_PARTICIPANT
        bool "Add a second (self-test) participant that calls the local servers"
        default n
        depends on RTPS_ENABLE_RPC
        help
            Additively bring up a SECOND RtpsParticipant on the device, with its
            own typed ServiceClient + ActionClient, that call THIS device's own
            /add_two_ints service and /fibonacci action. A participant filters out
            its own messages, so this is the only way to fully round-trip the
            client APIs on one device with no external peer - a self-contained
            self-test. Off by default: a second participant roughly doubles the
            RTPS engine's RAM (two discovery stacks, socket sets, and pools), which
            may not fit on a plain ESP32 without PSRAM. Independent of the
            peer-facing client demo, which always runs.

endmenu
